WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:01.801 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show,"

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.304
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.705 align:start position:0%
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:10.243
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:13.580 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, guys, after
seven months of negotiations,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.982 align:start size:88% position:13%
late Friday night,
the House finally passed

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.551 align:start size:84% position:16%
President Biden's
infrastructure deal.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.653 align:start size:81% position:19%
Yeah. So that's
obviously -- Yeah.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:88% position:13%
So, obviously --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:27.694
That's probably what everyone
was talking about this weekend.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.262
- Big Bird is causing a stir.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.497
- Big bird announced he was

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.998 align:start size:81% position:19%
getting vaccinated
against COVID.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.967 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Big Bird got his COVID shot
over the weekend.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.069
- Big Bird announces
he's been vaccinated.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.704
- Big Bird got the jab.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:41.975 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Somehow, that was
the big story this weekend --

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:45.678 align:start size:88% position:13%
Big Bird tweeting
that he got vaccinated.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.014
Yep.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.984 align:start size:88% position:13%
It was a big day,
actually, for Big Bird,

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
because immediately
after getting vaccinated,

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.587 align:start size:84% position:16%
he was signed by
the Green Bay Packers.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.789
So that is amazing.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:59.459 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's amazing to see
that career.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.129
Some more COVID news.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.098 align:start size:88% position:13%
Today, the U.S.
lifted the travel ban on

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:08.401 align:start size:97% position:3%
vaccinated tourists
for more than 30 countries.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.637
Of course, all the airports
are going to be slammed.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.838
Flight attendants were like,

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.940 align:start size:84% position:16%
"We're going to need
more duct tape."

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.043 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's right -- travelers are
thrilled to be back.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the first time people
ever cried tears of joy

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.980
at the sight of LaGuardia.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.219 align:start position:0%
That's right -- New York City is
expecting tens of thousands

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:30.090
of tourists, and they're all
going to walk in front of you.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.093
"Oh, wow."

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
19 months for a travel ban
is a long time.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:38.231
Yep, your friend who left to
study abroad in January 2020

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.300 align:start size:88% position:13%
actually came back
speaking fluent Italian.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.268
- Oh!

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.603 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, as I mentioned,
on Friday night,

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.539 align:start size:88% position:13%
the House passed Biden's
infrastructure bill.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.007
The bill took forever to pass.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:84% position:16%
When it was over,
they wrapped Biden in

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.678
a foil marathon blanket
and gave him a medal.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:54.247
They go...

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.716 align:start position:0%
Yeah, only 13 House Republicans
voted for the bill,

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:84% position:16%
while the rest said,
"We think that

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.320 align:start size:84% position:16%
if you're driving over
a collapsed bridge,

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:97% position:3%
you can just speed up
and you'll probably make it."

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:04.858 align:start size:84% position:16%
"You guys ever seen
the documentary

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.526
'Fast and the Furious?'"

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:10.763
Some business news.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.665
Walmart just announced
that it is now using

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.969 align:start position:0%
fully driverless trucks to
deliver groceries to customers.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.036
- Ooh.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.571
- It's pretty cool, actually.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.274 align:start position:0%
The driverless trucks
will pick up items from Walmart

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:24.911 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then deliver them right
through your living-room wall.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.180
What?!

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.481
- Oh, yeah!

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.482
- Oh, yeah!

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.651 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Oh, yeah!
- Yeah.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:34.454 align:start position:0%
Walmart is the only place you'll
find cutting-edge technology

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:37.624
and also a barefoot guy
buying margarita mix.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:39.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm surprised
it's not more packed here

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.928
at 3:00 in the morning."

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.330
Hey, I saw that,
guys, restaurants

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.932
are facing a shortage because of

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.268 align:start size:84% position:16%
supply-chain issues
of takeout containers.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:49.769
- Ooh!

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.704
- Yeah, that will be fun when
the Uber Eats guy is like,

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:54.507
"Here's your fries.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.876
Put it on your lap
or you want it..."

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.346 align:start size:97% position:3%
But this is
a huge problem for McDonald's,

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.581
because they actually make

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.216 align:start size:84% position:16%
McRibs out of
takeout containers.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.984 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Really?
- That's what I heard.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.587 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's what I heard.
I don't know.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:97% position:3%
Hey, I saw that,
in a recent Instagram post,

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:13.026 align:start position:0%
Vin Diesel called Dwayne Johnson
his "little brother"

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:16.796 align:start position:0%
and asked him to return to
the "Fast &amp; Furious" franchise.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.599 align:start size:97% position:3%
Yeah. It turns out Vin Diesel
also left a voicemail

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:22.235
to follow up with him, and we
actually got our hands on it.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.704 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Oh, my gosh!
- You guys want to hear it?

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:27.774 align:start size:97% position:3%
[ Cheers and applause ]
I mean, this is an exclusive.

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.609
Let's take a listen. Vin Diesel.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.187
[ Beep ]

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.296
[ Cheers and applause ]
- We got the exclusive.

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.398
We got it tonight.

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.666
Wow.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:32.105 align:start position:0%
And, finally, the New York City
Marathon was this weekend.

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:35.742 align:start position:0%
Congrats to anyone who raced it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.010
Amazing.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:41.481 align:start position:0%
I read that one guy ran 17 miles
with an engagement ring

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:43.549
and then proposed to his
girlfriend during the race.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.717
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
What's more romantic
than proposing

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
next to Times Square Elmo
peeing his costume?

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:51.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, that's...
It actually was very cute.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:52.225
They even celebrated with

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:54.127 align:start size:84% position:16%
tiny paper cups
filled with champagne.

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.297 align:start size:84% position:16%
Some big entertainment
news, actually --

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:59.565 align:start size:97% position:3%
the creator of "Squid Game"
announced

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.534 align:start size:84% position:16%
that Season 2 is now
in the works.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.069
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.171
That‘s right, season 1 left
so many unanswered questions,

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.573 align:start position:0%
like, "I loved this show.
What the hell is wrong with me?"

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.075
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:11.277 align:start size:97% position:3%
Even the creator of the "Saw"
franchise is like,

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.879 align:start size:97% position:3%
"I‘m not sure how much more
of this we can take."

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:14.314
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.282
Yeah, all your favorite
characters will be back,

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:17.750
like Player 456

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and cheering ]
and...

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.486 align:start size:84% position:16%
well, that‘s about it.
Everyone else...

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.954
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.090
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.060
Yep, "Squid Game" is the most
dangerous game you can play.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.595
Well, other than football
with Aaron Rodgers, but --

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.564
[ Laughter, ohs, and applause ]

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.166 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Oh.
- Oh, fine.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.467
You huddle with him, okay?

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.402
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.470
Some more entertainment news --

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.505 align:start size:88% position:13%
I read that,
to compete with TikTok,

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:43.176 align:start size:97% position:3%
Netflix is rolling out
a feature called Kids Clips,

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:45.111
which will show short videos

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:47.747 align:start size:97% position:3%
from their library
of children‘s content, yeah.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.582 align:start size:84% position:16%
It‘s Netflix‘s version
of TikTok,

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.718 align:start position:0%
that‘s why, every three seconds,
a message pops up that says,

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:52.785
"Are you still watching?"

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.220
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, this is exciting --
last night,

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:59.158 align:start size:97% position:3%
after 200 days in orbit,
four astronauts splashed down

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:02.428 align:start size:88% position:13%
in the Gulf of Mexico
aboard a SpaceX capsule.

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.397
Yep, 200 days in space.

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:05.598
After landing they said,

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:06.699 align:start size:97% position:3%
"We were going a little crazy
up there.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:07.967 align:start size:88% position:13%
At one point,
we looked out the window

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.268
and I swear we saw
William Shatner."

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.671
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.239
Wild.

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:15.575 align:start position:0%
- Ooh.
- Of course, this SpaceX mission

00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:18.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
made headlines because the
toilet onboard broke

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.613 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the astronauts had
to wear diapers.

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:22.882
[ Audience ohs ] So, when
they splashed down, they...

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:25.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Groaning and laughter ]
- Oh!

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:26.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheering and applause ]
- Really.

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:27.754
[ Rimshot ]

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:29.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
They really splashed down,
yeah.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
Meanwhile, Virgin Galactic
just announced

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:34.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it now has
about 700 paying customers

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:37.463 align:start size:97% position:3%
who are waiting to go to space
on its commercial flight.

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:38.998
Of course, since it‘s Virgin,

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.767 align:start size:97% position:3%
the first trip will only last
two minutes.

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.735
[ Laughter, ohs, and applause ]

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:43.970 align:start size:97% position:3%
The headline
can definitely be improved,

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:44.904
because if you only
look at the photo,

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:45.037
the headline could have been...

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:48.574 align:start size:84% position:16%
That‘s normal
for space exploration.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:51.144
- It takes a while
to get into space.

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:52.945 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Get this --
customers will soon be able

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:55.982 align:start size:84% position:16%
to earn Bitcoin
every time they dine

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.918 align:start size:88% position:13%
at Bubba Gump Shrimp
and the Rainforest Cafe.

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:00.520
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.155 align:start size:97% position:3%
Right now, parents are like,
"What‘s Bitcoin?",

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:03.790
while kids are like,
"Who‘s Bubba Gump?"

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.058
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.961 align:start size:97% position:3%
Hey, I saw that a man
in the UK has found a new way

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:11.197 align:start size:97% position:3%
to help people get around
and make a little extra money

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:12.465
on the side.
Watch this.

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:14.267
- It‘s called the Tank Taxi.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:16.736 align:start size:97% position:3%
Merlin Batchelor is the guy
behind the wheel.

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:18.504
He bought that vehicle online

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.174 align:start size:97% position:3%
and now, requests for rides
in it are rolling in.

00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:23.009 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Right now,
Merlin is only licensed

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:25.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
to carry passengers
for weddings and funerals.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:29.615
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:31.217
- Funerals?

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.618
- Or having a wedding.

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.120 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like who‘s --
- Or even a wedding.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.621
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:38.291
I love that people are rolling
up to a funeral in a tank like,

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:39.625
"It‘s what Grandpa
would‘ve wanted.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.828
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:43.062
He wasn‘t even in the service.

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:44.430 align:start size:84% position:16%
He just liked
‘Call of Duty,‘ yeah."

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:47.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.002
Finally, a car parked
on an Italian street

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:52.038 align:start position:0%
has become a tourist attraction
because it‘s been

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:54.841 align:start size:75% position:25%
in the same spot
for 47 years.

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:56.142
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:57.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
Meanwhile,
there‘s a 95-year-old guy

00:07:57.677 --> 00:07:59.245
wandering the neighborhood
like, "I know I parked it

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:00.713 align:start size:75% position:25%
here somewhere."
[ Applause ]

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:03.349 align:start size:97% position:3%
Guys, it seems like there‘s so
much going on right now.

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:06.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
The supply chain is still
causing problems.

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:08.254
Paul Rudd was named
"Sexiest Man Alive".

00:08:08.254 --> 00:08:11.424
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:11.424 --> 00:08:13.926
Adele debuted a new song.

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:15.828
[ Cheers ]

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:19.065
And Arby‘s just announced two
French fry flavored vodkas.

00:08:19.065 --> 00:08:21.934 align:start size:97% position:3%
[ Laughter ]
There‘s just a lot to go over.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.436 align:start position:0%
So let‘s just jump in and cover
it all at once.

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:25.738 align:start size:97% position:3%
It‘s time for a "News Smash."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:25.738 --> 00:08:29.675
♪

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:31.677
First up, the supply chain.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.913 align:start size:97% position:3%
President Biden just met with
several companies

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:36.349 align:start position:0%
like Walmart, Target, and FedEx
to discuss solutions

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:38.084
and it‘s not looking great.

00:08:38.084 --> 00:08:39.886 align:start size:84% position:16%
But, you know
who is looking great?

00:08:39.886 --> 00:08:41.320 align:start size:88% position:13%
Paul Rudd.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:44.624 align:start position:0%
He was named "People‘s"
Sexiest Man Alive. Good for him.

00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:47.093
He‘s universally beloved.
He makes us all laugh.

00:08:47.093 --> 00:08:49.228
But if you prefer someone
who‘s universally beloved

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:52.064
and makes us all cry,
there‘s always Adele.

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:54.267 align:start size:97% position:3%
[ Cheers and applause ]
She just debuted a new song

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:57.036 align:start position:0%
