and it‘s fantastic.

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:59.438 align:start size:97% position:3%
The song is called "Hold On,"
and it‘s all about

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:00.940
not giving up.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.643 align:start size:97% position:3%
But if you want to give up,
why not try Arby‘s new

00:09:03.643 --> 00:09:06.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
French fry vodka.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:08.614 align:start size:97% position:3%
They‘re releasing two bottles,
and apparently,

00:09:08.614 --> 00:09:10.650
they have the same
"flavor profile"

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.985 align:start size:84% position:16%
as their curly
and crinkle-cut fries.

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:14.420
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don‘t understand
how that would even work.

00:09:16.422 --> 00:09:19.125
Speaking of things I don‘t
understand, the supply chain.

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:22.094 align:start size:97% position:3%
[ Laughter ]
Shipping, trucking, inflation,

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:23.629 align:start size:97% position:3%
all of it has people really
stressed out.

00:09:23.629 --> 00:09:25.197
But it‘s going to be okay.

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:28.067
Just take a deep breath,
pour yourself some wine

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:29.168 align:start size:84% position:16%
and listen to Adele.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.168 --> 00:09:31.304
The new album drops next week.

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:33.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her first album was "19,"
loved that.

00:09:33.606 --> 00:09:36.776
[ Cheers and applause ]
Then "21," loved that.

00:09:36.776 --> 00:09:39.845
[ Cheers and applause ]
Then "25," and now "30."

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:41.814 align:start size:97% position:3%
[ Cheers and applause ]
We‘re really -- we‘ve really

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:43.482
seen her grow up over the years.

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:44.817
You know who hasn‘t grown up?

00:09:44.817 --> 00:09:46.052 align:start size:88% position:13%
Paul Rudd.
I mean, look at the guy.

00:09:46.052 --> 00:09:47.320
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
He -- he only gets better
with age.

00:09:49.889 --> 00:09:51.724
You know what doesn‘t
get better with age?

00:09:51.724 --> 00:09:53.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
Arby‘s vodka.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:53.893 --> 00:09:55.595
I -- I just don‘t get it.

00:09:55.595 --> 00:09:57.930 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, from the vodka itself
to the label,

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.132 align:start size:97% position:3%
all the way to the bottleneck.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:01.834 align:start size:84% position:16%
Everything‘s
completely backed up.

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.636
So it‘ll affect prices.

00:10:03.636 --> 00:10:04.937
And if you order
anything online,

00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
be prepared to "hold on."
[ Laughter ]

00:10:07.073 --> 00:10:10.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
In conclusion, what a guy.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:11.310
Time to cry,

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:12.812
low supply,

00:10:12.812 --> 00:10:14.246 align:start size:72% position:28%
just why?
[ Laughter ]

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:15.748 align:start size:97% position:3%
This has been a "News Smash"!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:20.753
♪

00:10:21.921 --> 00:10:23.656
Thank you.

00:10:23.656 --> 00:10:24.857
Hey, here‘s some COVID news.

00:10:24.857 --> 00:10:26.425 align:start size:84% position:16%
Apparently,
the U.S. government

00:10:26.425 --> 00:10:28.761 align:start size:84% position:16%
helped Moderna
develop their vaccine.

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:30.730 align:start size:81% position:19%
And now they‘re in
a patent fight

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.199
over who deserves credit for it.

00:10:33.199 --> 00:10:35.067
Yeah, even crazier, they‘re
going to settle it on a --

00:10:35.067 --> 00:10:38.604 align:start size:97% position:3%
with a rap battle on "VERZUZ."
[ Laughter ]

00:10:38.604 --> 00:10:39.972 align:start size:84% position:16%
Meanwhile,
there‘s also a battle

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:42.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
over the Johnson &amp; Johnson
patent because

00:10:42.074 --> 00:10:43.342 align:start size:84% position:16%
nobody wants to
take credit for it.

00:10:43.342 --> 00:10:45.711 align:start size:97% position:3%
[ Laughter ]
No, it was the other Johnson.

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:47.880 align:start size:84% position:16%
[ Laughter ]
Some business news.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:50.883 align:start size:97% position:3%
YouTube just announced that it
is hiding dislike counts

00:10:50.883 --> 00:10:53.352
on all videos.
That‘s right.

00:10:53.352 --> 00:10:55.187 align:start size:88% position:13%
Now instead of clicking
thumbs down,

00:10:55.187 --> 00:10:57.156 align:start position:0%
people will just write "dislike"
in the comments.

00:10:57.156 --> 00:10:59.692
[ Laughter ]
"Not for me."

00:10:59.692 --> 00:11:02.495 align:start size:84% position:16%
[ Laughter ]
Yep, no more dislikes.

00:11:02.495 --> 00:11:05.164 align:start size:97% position:3%
Instead, YouTube will provide
the user‘s home address

00:11:05.164 --> 00:11:06.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you can just tell them
in person

00:11:06.432 --> 00:11:08.934 align:start position:0%
how much you hated their video.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:08.934 --> 00:11:10.503
Yeah, dislikes are annoying.

00:11:10.503 --> 00:11:12.338
They‘re right up there with
people who comment "first!"

00:11:12.338 --> 00:11:14.440 align:start size:84% position:16%
It‘s like,
"Oh, it‘s just stop."

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.841 align:start size:81% position:19%
Well, the holidays
are coming up,

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:17.677 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I read that ‘cause of the
tight labor market,

00:11:17.677 --> 00:11:20.579 align:start size:97% position:3%
there‘s actually a shortage
of mall Santas.

00:11:20.579 --> 00:11:22.281
[ Audience "aws" ]

00:11:22.281 --> 00:11:24.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, malls are desperate
to find Santas.

00:11:24.517 --> 00:11:26.652 align:start position:0%
Today, in fact, Macy‘s put out a
bowl of whiskey

00:11:26.652 --> 00:11:29.321 align:start position:0%
outside the store like they were
trying to lure a stray cat.

00:11:29.321 --> 00:11:33.559 align:start size:72% position:28%
[ Laughter ]
- Wow.

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:34.960 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Putting a bowl of whiskey
out there.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
- For Santas.
Yeah, it‘s hard to recruit

00:11:37.096 --> 00:11:38.664 align:start size:84% position:16%
for the job,
because you can‘t just

00:11:38.664 --> 00:11:40.533
walk up to people like, "Hey,
you‘re built like Santa Claus.

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:43.769 align:start size:81% position:19%
Do you want to --"
[ Laughter ]

00:11:43.769 --> 00:11:45.271
That‘s right.
No mall Santas.

00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:46.839 align:start size:97% position:3%
Instead,
it‘ll just be an elf saying,

00:11:46.839 --> 00:11:48.240
"Whatever you want, it‘s on
Amazon. Merry Christmas."

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.442
[ Laughter ]

00:11:49.442 --> 00:11:50.976 align:start size:84% position:16%
Hey, get this,
The Hallmark Channel

00:11:50.976 --> 00:11:54.280 align:start size:97% position:3%
is holding a baking contest
and the grand prize is

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:59.251 align:start size:97% position:3%
a walk-on role in a Hallmark
original movie or $5,000.

00:11:59.885 --> 00:12:01.153
[ Laughter ]

00:12:01.153 --> 00:12:02.555
Even the director of the
Hallmark movie was like,

00:12:02.555 --> 00:12:05.725 align:start size:81% position:19%
"Take the money!"
[ Laughter ]

00:12:05.725 --> 00:12:08.160
Seriously, for 5 grand, you can
shoot your own hallmark movie.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.229
- Yeah.

00:12:10.229 --> 00:12:13.099
- Hey, here‘s good news, the
North American Meat Institute

00:12:13.099 --> 00:12:14.600 align:start size:81% position:19%
said it will reach
Paris Agreement

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.836
emission targets by 2030.

00:12:16.836 --> 00:12:18.237 align:start size:84% position:16%
When I heard,
my first thought was,

00:12:18.237 --> 00:12:20.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
"There‘s a North American
Meat Institute?"

00:12:20.072 --> 00:12:22.074 align:start size:88% position:13%
[ Laughter ]
Sounds less like a real

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:23.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
organization and more like
something you‘d read

00:12:23.743 --> 00:12:25.611 align:start size:84% position:16%
on the shirt of a dude
at CrossFit.

00:12:25.611 --> 00:12:29.215
[ Laughter ]

00:12:29.215 --> 00:12:30.483
It‘s a long walk
but it‘s worth it.

00:12:30.483 --> 00:12:32.118 align:start size:88% position:13%
I like that joke. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:32.118 --> 00:12:33.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
And finally,
according to new research,

00:12:33.753 --> 00:12:35.788 align:start size:97% position:3%
it‘s perfect --
the perfect time to go to bed

00:12:35.788 --> 00:12:40.659
for your heart‘s health is
between 10:00 and 11:00 P.M.

00:12:40.659 --> 00:12:42.862 align:start position:0%
Probably explains why NBC ran a
promo today that said,

00:12:42.862 --> 00:12:44.697 align:start position:0%
"Forget your heart and catch an
all-new episode of

00:12:44.697 --> 00:12:45.831
‘The Tonight Show.‘"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:46.866 --> 00:12:48.868 align:start size:84% position:16%
You guys,
it is Veterans Day,

00:12:48.868 --> 00:12:51.237 align:start size:97% position:3%
and, tonight,
our entire audience is made up

00:12:51.237 --> 00:12:55.207 align:start size:97% position:3%
of veterans, active military,
and military families.

00:12:55.207 --> 00:12:58.878
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:58.878 --> 00:13:03.783
♪

00:13:04.517 --> 00:13:05.785
Please, have a seat.

00:13:05.785 --> 00:13:07.386
Welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome.

00:13:07.386 --> 00:13:10.456
That‘s right. It‘s just like our
Fleet Week audience but sober.

00:13:11.056 --> 00:13:13.726
[ Laughter ]

00:13:13.726 --> 00:13:16.228 align:start position:0%
All kidding aside, I want to say
thank you for your service.

00:13:16.228 --> 00:13:19.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
You truly are the bravest.
Thank you.

00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:20.833
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:20.833 --> 00:13:24.503 align:start position:0%
I mean it.
The closest most of us have come

00:13:24.503 --> 00:13:27.540
to a war zone is shopping
on Black Friday at TJ Maxx.

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:28.941 align:start size:81% position:19%
[ Laughter ]
"Give that to me!

00:13:28.941 --> 00:13:30.876
It‘s not even my size."

00:13:30.876 --> 00:13:33.512
Yep, the only people who have
seen more combat than you guys

00:13:33.512 --> 00:13:35.514 align:start size:84% position:16%
are flight attendants
on Southwest.

00:13:35.514 --> 00:13:39.251
[ Laughter ]

00:13:39.251 --> 00:13:42.021 align:start position:0%
I remember -- I remember telling
my dad that I thought

00:13:42.021 --> 00:13:44.190 align:start size:84% position:16%
a life in uniform
might be right for me,

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:46.725 align:start position:0%
so he went out and got me
a job application for Pizza Hut.

00:13:46.725 --> 00:13:49.195 align:start size:72% position:28%
[ Laughter ]
- Oh.

00:13:49.195 --> 00:13:51.597 align:start size:84% position:16%
Sadly, they said no.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:51.597 --> 00:13:54.033
Of course, the Space Force
couldn‘t be here tonight.

00:13:54.033 --> 00:13:55.634
They‘re busy --
[ Laughter ]

00:13:55.634 --> 00:14:00.539
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.680
They‘re busy monitoring
the galaxy for missiles,

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:10.249 align:start size:97% position:3%
aliens, and our newest threat,
bored billionaires.

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:14.186
[ Laughter ]

00:14:14.186 --> 00:14:16.956 align:start size:97% position:3%
A lot of restaurants
offered special deals today.

00:14:16.956 --> 00:14:19.892 align:start position:0%
Servicemembers could get a free
bloomin‘ onion at Outback.

00:14:19.892 --> 00:14:21.627
[ Cheers ]

00:14:21.627 --> 00:14:24.063 align:start size:84% position:16%
Free pancakes at IHOP.
[ Cheers ]

00:14:24.063 --> 00:14:25.764
And a free doughnut
at Krispy Kreme.

00:14:25.764 --> 00:14:27.266
[ Cheers ]

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:29.034 align:start size:97% position:3%
And if you ate all three,
we have an ambulance outside

00:14:29.034 --> 00:14:31.837 align:start size:97% position:3%
standing by, so don‘t worry.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:14:31.837 --> 00:14:33.305
Let‘s get to the news.

00:14:33.305 --> 00:14:36.075 align:start position:0%
The Postmaster General just said
that the U.S. Postal Service

00:14:36.075 --> 00:14:39.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
is ready for
the holiday-package rush.

00:14:39.078 --> 00:14:40.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
Unfortunately, the holiday
they‘re talking about

00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:41.814
is July 4th.
[ Laughter ]

00:14:41.814 --> 00:14:44.049
But still, they‘re ready.

00:14:44.049 --> 00:14:46.385 align:start size:97% position:3%
That‘s right.
The post office is prepared,

00:14:46.385 --> 00:14:48.120 align:start position:0%
meaning they "prepared" hundreds
of signs that say

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:50.723 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Next window please."
[ Laughter ]

00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:52.658
That‘s right. They said that
they‘re ready for the rush.

00:14:52.658 --> 00:14:54.894 align:start position:0%
Although I don‘t know how I feel
about the new slogan,

00:14:54.894 --> 00:14:57.496
"United States Postal Service:
We can handle your package."

00:14:57.496 --> 00:14:58.998 align:start size:72% position:28%
[ Laughter ]
- Oh.

00:14:58.998 --> 00:15:00.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
- You can‘t say that.
- Why would you say that?

00:15:00.399 --> 00:15:02.768 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You can‘t say that anymore.
You can‘t --

00:15:02.768 --> 00:15:04.737
♪

00:15:04.737 --> 00:15:07.339
- Package.

00:15:07.339 --> 00:15:09.808 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Some business news.
The tuna lawsuit

00:15:09.808 --> 00:15:12.711 align:start size:88% position:13%
against Subway,
the sandwiches, is back.

00:15:12.711 --> 00:15:16.348
Yeah, and now, they‘re saying
that the tuna contains chicken,

00:15:16.348 --> 00:15:19.818
pork, and cattle DNA.
[ Audience groans ]

00:15:19.818 --> 00:15:22.254 align:start size:97% position:3%
Even crazier, when they tested
Subway‘s chicken and pork,

00:15:22.254 --> 00:15:24.089 align:start size:97% position:3%
they found it was 100% tuna.
- Really?

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:27.693
[ Laughter ]

00:15:27.693 --> 00:15:30.296 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yep, chicken, pork,
and cattle DNA.

00:15:30.296 --> 00:15:31.530
Right now, Subway‘s thinking,

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:33.232 align:start size:88% position:13%
"All things considered,
not bad."

00:15:33.232 --> 00:15:34.667
[ Laughter ]

00:15:34.667 --> 00:15:36.135
"They‘re all meats, right?"

00:15:36.135 --> 00:15:38.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yep, Subway‘s like,
"What do you want from us?

00:15:38.203 --> 00:15:40.039 align:start size:88% position:13%
It‘s fish served
with an ice-cream scoop.

00:15:40.039 --> 00:15:41.240 align:start size:81% position:19%
Come on.
What do you want?"

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:42.841 align:start size:88% position:13%
[ Laughter ]
It‘s not like Morimoto‘s

00:15:42.841 --> 00:15:45.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
sharpening his knives
back there, cutting it up.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:49.748
[ Laughter ]

00:15:49.748 --> 00:15:53.118 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, I read that the CEO
of Royal Caribbean said that

00:15:53.118 --> 00:15:55.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
the company is seeing
historically strong bookings

00:15:55.287 --> 00:15:57.389
for cruises next summer.

00:15:57.389 --> 00:15:58.958 align:start size:88% position:13%
Right now, members of
the Coast Guard and Navy

00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:00.192
are looking at each other, like,

00:16:00.192 --> 00:16:02.027 align:start position:0%
"So, you guys gonna handle this,
or should we?"

00:16:02.027 --> 00:16:03.696
[ Laughter ]

00:16:03.696 --> 00:16:05.764 align:start size:97% position:3%
Meanwhile, Carnival Cruises
still hasn‘t let people

00:16:05.764 --> 00:16:07.533
off the boats from March 2020.

00:16:07.533 --> 00:16:10.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
"No, not yet.

00:16:10.269 --> 00:16:12.404
Not looking good.

00:16:12.404 --> 00:16:14.907
More tuna!"
[ Laughter ]

00:16:14.907 --> 00:16:16.575 align:start size:97% position:3%
That‘s right, Royal Caribbean
said it‘s expecting

00:16:16.575 --> 00:16:19.178 align:start size:97% position:3%
record profits,
and then the CEO of Imodium

00:16:19.178 --> 00:16:24.183 align:start size:84% position:16%
was like, "Same here."
[ Laughter ]

00:16:25.084 --> 00:16:27.152 align:start size:72% position:28%
Some --
[ Chuckles ]

00:16:27.152 --> 00:16:29.121 align:start size:84% position:16%
Some air -- thank you.
Some airline --

00:16:29.121 --> 00:16:31.523
Some airline news.
The FAA has proposed

00:16:31.523 --> 00:16:36.528
more than $200,000 in fines
for 10 unruly passengers.

00:16:37.529 --> 00:16:38.897 align:start size:81% position:19%
Yeah.
And this is nice.

00:16:38.897 --> 00:16:40.132 align:start size:97% position:3%
Starting today,
if you‘re flying from Florida,

00:16:40.132 --> 00:16:42.034
they ask if you want
to pre-pay your fine.

00:16:42.034 --> 00:16:44.837 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Aww.
[ Laughter ]

00:16:44.837 --> 00:16:47.439 align:start position:0%
- "Hold my -- Hold my Four Loko.
That‘s unbelievable!"

00:16:47.439 --> 00:16:49.975
[ Laughter ]

00:16:49.975 --> 00:16:52.578 align:start size:97% position:3%
Get this -- I read that
a new survey found that 80%

00:16:52.578 --> 00:16:55.581 align:start size:97% position:3%
of Americans use slang words
but only half

00:16:55.581 --> 00:16:58.050
know what the slang terms
they use actually mean.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
[ Laughter ]
Those aren‘t great numbers,

00:16:59.752 --> 00:17:01.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I thought
I‘d help everyone brush up

00:17:01.153 --> 00:17:03.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
on their slang definitions
with a tiny song.

00:17:03.655 --> 00:17:08.660
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:16.001
[ Tapping ]

00:17:16.001 --> 00:17:19.972 align:start size:84% position:16%
♪ Acting extra ♪
means "over the top" ♪

00:17:19.972 --> 00:17:23.642 align:start size:97% position:3%
♪ Spill the tea means ♪
you should share the goss ♪

00:17:23.642 --> 00:17:25.044
♪ Receipts are proof ♪

00:17:25.044 --> 00:17:27.746 align:start size:97% position:3%
♪ If you seem sus, ♪
sus is short for suspicious ♪

00:17:27.746 --> 00:17:30.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪ Gucci‘s cool ♪
and flex is showing off ♪

00:17:30.082 --> 00:17:31.550
[ Laughter ]

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:35.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
♪ Curves is when you ignore ♪
a flirty text ♪

00:17:35.287 --> 00:17:39.058 align:start size:97% position:3%
♪ No cap means "for real," ♪
"We move" means "yes" ♪

00:17:39.058 --> 00:17:40.793 align:start size:88% position:13%
♪ Simping‘s ♪
when you like someone ♪

00:17:40.793 --> 00:17:42.728
♪ But do too much for them ♪

00:17:42.728 --> 00:17:45.364 align:start size:97% position:3%
♪ And simps are almost stans ♪
but just not -- ♪

00:17:45.364 --> 00:17:47.599 align:start size:97% position:3%
Dang! Sorry.
Let me do it one more time.

00:17:47.599 --> 00:17:50.536
Can I do it one more time?
Hoo! All right, I‘m close.

00:17:50.536 --> 00:17:52.071
[ Laughter ]

00:17:52.071 --> 00:17:53.772
Yeah, don‘t waste your time
clapping because who knows

00:17:53.772 --> 00:17:54.973
how many takes
I got to do this.

00:17:54.973 --> 00:17:57.376
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:17:57.376 --> 00:17:59.411 align:start size:84% position:16%
Be exhausted.
- Go wash your hands.

00:17:59.411 --> 00:18:03.515
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:18:03.515 --> 00:18:05.517 align:start position:0%
